### Downstream Breaking Changes

<a id="finding-pr-42435-pageable-sdk-shape"></a>
### Generated SDK result changes to a pageable abstraction

- **Severity:** medium
- **Confidence:** high
- **Summary:** Although the REST response already contains value and nextLink, adding paging metadata can change the generated method's public return type, iteration protocol, and continuation behavior, breaking source code that consumes the prior non-pageable LRO result.
- **Evidence:** Each AutoRest diff adds only x-ms-pageable.nextLinkName = nextLink to OutboundRules_Post.; Generated clients now expose the existing LRO result as pageable, using value as the item collection and nextLink as the continuation link.
- **TypeSpec source:** [ManagedNetworkSettingsPropertiesBasicResource.tsp:L81-L87](https://github.com/Azure/azure-rest-api-specs/blob/96eae0e7d5c7ede040ee0cc646d397e5d8375912/specification/cognitiveservices/CognitiveServices.Management/ManagedNetworkSettingsPropertiesBasicResource.tsp#L81-L87)


